  "output": "## Test coverage analysis — Canon web app\n\n**Baseline finding:** there is no test infrastructure at all — no test runner in `package.json`, no config, zero `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*` files anywhere in the repo. Every gap below is therefore \"100% untested.\" I've grouped findings by module with a skeleton per gap. Recommended stack (none currently installed): **Vitest** (+ `@testing-library/react`, `jsdom`) for units/components, **Playwright** for integration/e2e — `playwright-cli` skill is already available in this environment.\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react jsdom @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom @playwright/test\n```\n\n---\n\n### A. `lib/cn.ts` — `cn()`\nUntested. No edge cases for conflicting Tailwind classes, falsy inputs, or arrays.\n\n```ts\n// lib/cn.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/cn\";\n\ndescribe(\"cn\", () => {\n  it(\"merges plain class strings\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"a\", \"b\")).toBe(\"a b\");\n  });\n  it(\"drops falsy values\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"a\", false, undefined, null, \"b\")).toBe(\"a b\");\n  });\n  it(\"lets the later conflicting Tailwind class win\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"px-2\", \"px-4\")).toBe(\"px-4\");\n  });\n  it(\"flattens arrays/objects (clsx semantics)\", () => {\n    expect(cn([\"a\", { b: true, c: false }])).toBe(\"a b\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### B. `types/rules.ts` — `ruleSpecificity()`\nThe only non-schema pure function in `types/`. Untested, and its ordering contract (\"most specific first\") is load-bearing for survivorship resolution — a regression here silently changes which rule wins.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity, type SurvivorshipRule } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\nconst rule = (field: string, entityType: string): SurvivorshipRule => ({\n  id: \"r1\", field, entityType, strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"\",\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"scores exact field + exact entityType highest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"name\", \"account\"))).toBe(3);\n  });\n  it(\"scores wildcard field, exact entityType\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"*\", \"account\"))).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"scores exact field, wildcard entityType\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"name\", \"*\"))).toBe(2);\n  });\n  it(\"scores full wildcard lowest\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity(rule(\"*\", \"*\"))).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"sorts a rule set most-specific-first\", () => {\n    const rules = [rule(\"*\", \"*\"), rule(\"name\", \"account\"), rule(\"*\", \"account\")];\n    const sorted = [...rules].sort((a, b) => ruleSpecificity(b) - ruleSpecificity(a));\n    expect(sorted[0]).toBe(rules[1]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Missing error handling / edge case:** `survivorshipRuleSchema`'s `.refine` (strategy `prefer_source` requires `preferredSourceId`) is completely untested — it's the one cross-field invariant in the type layer.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts (continued)\nimport { survivorshipRuleSchema } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema refine\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source with no preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\",\n      strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.error?.issues[0].path).toEqual([\"preferredSourceId\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId set\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\",\n      strategy: \"prefer_source\", preferredSourceId: \"src-a\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### C. Zod schemas (`types/*.ts`) — validation boundaries\nThese are the \"tool contract\" schemas the codebase's own comments say must mirror `engine/pipeline/schema.py`. None are tested, so nothing catches drift between the two sides, and nothing documents what a malformed payload does.\n\nGaps: `sourceConfigSchema` (`objects` empty array rejected — `.min(1)`), `severitySchema` (rejects `0`/`5`), `reviewActionSchema` discriminated union (unknown `action`, `override` with empty `overrideValue`), `runStatsSchema` (negative/float ints), `sourceSchema.createdAt` coercion from string vs Date vs invalid string.\n\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { sourceConfigSchema, createSourceSchema, sourceSchema } from \"@/types/source\";\n\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty objects array\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts config without an optional filter\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects a name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    const result = createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"x\".repeat(81), kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown kind\", () => {\n    const result = createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"CRM\", kind: \"postgres\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"sourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"coerces createdAt from an ISO string\", () => {\n    const parsed = sourceSchema.parse({\n      id: \"9c858901-8a57-4791-81fe-4c455b099bc9\",\n      name: \"CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n      createdAt: \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n    });\n    expect(parsed.createdAt).toBeInstanceOf(Date);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects a non-uuid id\", () => {\n    expect(sourceSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"not-a-uuid\", name: \"CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n      config: { objects: [\"Account\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/conflict.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { severitySchema } from \"@/types/conflict\";\n\ndescribe(\"severitySchema\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4])(\"accepts %i\", (v) => expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(true));\n  it.each([0, 5, 2.5, \"3\"])(\"rejects %p\", (v) => expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(false));\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/resolution.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewActionSchema } from \"@/types/resolution\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts approve/reject with no extra fields\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects override with an empty overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown action\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"delete\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### D. `lib/db/index.ts` — `getDb()`\n**Missing error handling test** — this is the one function with an explicit `throw new Error(...)`, and it's completely unexercised.\n\n```ts\n// lib/db/index.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.resetModules();\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonDb;\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonSql;\n    delete process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"caches the client on globalThis across calls (HMR-safe)\", async () => {\n    process.env.DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/db\";\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    const first = getDb();\n    const second = getDb();\n    expect(first).toBe(second);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### E. `lib/server/sources.ts` — `listSources()` / `countSourcesBySide()`\nBoth fully untested. Requires mocking `@/lib/db` (or an integration DB — see section K).\n\nGaps: `listSources` throwing when a DB row fails `sourceSchema.parse` (malformed `config.objects`, bad `kind`); `countSourcesBySide` with zero sources, with a `synthetic` source (counted in neither `crm` nor `warehouse`), and with sources of every kind mixed.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/server\", () => ({ connection: vi.fn() }));\nconst selectMock = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({\n  getDb: () => ({\n    select: () => ({ from: () => ({ orderBy: selectMock }) }),\n  }),\n}));\n\nconst row = (overrides: Partial<any> = {}) => ({\n  id: \"9c858901-8a57-4791-81fe-4c455b099bc9\",\n  name: \"CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n  createdAt: new Date(),\n  ...overrides,\n});\n\nbeforeEach(() => selectMock.mockReset());\n\ndescribe(\"listSources\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty array when no sources exist\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockResolvedValue([]);\n    const { listSources } = await import(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\n    expect(await listSources()).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when a stored row fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockResolvedValue([row({ kind: \"not-a-real-kind\" })]);\n    const { listSources } = await import(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\n    await expect(listSources()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets salesforce/hubspot as crm and databricks/snowflake as warehouse\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockResolvedValue([\n      row({ kind: \"salesforce\" }), row({ kind: \"hubspot\" }),\n      row({ kind: \"databricks\" }), row({ kind: \"snowflake\" }),\n      row({ kind: \"synthetic\" }),\n    ]);\n    const { countSourcesBySide } = await import(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\n    expect(await countSourcesBySide()).toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 2, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns all zeros with no sources configured\", async () => {\n    selectMock.mockResolvedValue([]);\n    const { countSourcesBySide } = await import(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\n    expect(await countSourcesBySide()).toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### F. Presentational components with real branching logic\n\n**`SeverityMark`** (`components/severity-mark.tsx`) — the `MARK`/`TREATMENT`/`SEVERITY_LABEL` record lookups are typed to `Severity` (1|2|3|4), but nothing guards a bad *runtime* value (e.g. a DB row bypassing the schema) — it would silently render `undefined`. Also untested: the \"never without its word\" invariant the comment calls out.\n\n```tsx\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"@/components/severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([\n    [4, \"Structural\"], [3, \"Attribute\"], [2, \"Attribute\"], [1, \"Cosmetic\"],\n  ] as const)(\"renders the label for severity %i\", (severity, label) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={severity} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(label)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"never renders the mark without its text label\", () => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={1} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"█░░░\").nextSibling ?? screen.getByText(\"Cosmetic\")).toBeTruthy();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`CanonMark`** — untested threshold behavior at `size <= 18` (stroke width 9 vs 7.5, radius 6.5 vs 6).\n\n```tsx\n// components/canon-mark.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { CanonMark } from \"@/components/canon-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"CanonMark\", () => {\n  it(\"uses the thick stroke at the default small size (20 is > 18)\", () => {\n    const { container } = render(<CanonMark />);\n    expect(container.querySelector(\"path\")).toHaveAttribute(\"stroke-width\", \"7.5\");\n  });\n  it(\"uses the extra-thick stroke at exactly the 18px threshold\", () => {\n    const { container } = render(<CanonMark size={18} />);\n    expect(container.querySelector(\"path\")).toHaveAttribute(\"stroke-width\", \"9\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`NavRail`** (`components/console/nav-rail.tsx`) — `pathname.startsWith(item.href)` for active-state detection is untested and has a real edge case: visiting `/sources/new` marks **Sources** active (arguably correct), but nothing pins that behavior down, and the root `/` route matches nothing.\n\n```tsx\n// components/console/nav-rail.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ usePathname: () => \"/sources/new\" }));\nimport { NavRail } from \"@/components/console/nav-rail\";\n\ndescribe(\"NavRail\", () => {\n  it(\"marks Sources active for a nested route like /sources/new\", () => {\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Sources\" })).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not mark unrelated links active\", () => {\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Runs\" })).not.toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`Button`** — `cva` variant/size matrix and `asChild` (Slot) behavior are untested.\n\n```tsx\n// components/ui/button.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n\ndescribe(\"Button\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults to the primary variant and md size\", () => {\n    render(<Button>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\")).toHaveClass(\"bg-g-900\", \"h-9\");\n  });\n  it(\"renders as the child element when asChild is set\", () => {\n    render(<Button asChild><a href=\"/x\">Link</a></Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\")).toHaveClass(\"bg-g-900\");\n  });\n  it(\"applies disabled styling and blocks pointer events\", () => {\n    render(<Button disabled>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\")).toBeDisabled();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### G. `SourceTable` / `SourcesEmptyState` / `SourcesPage` — untested rendering branches\n\nGaps: empty `sources` array (renders an empty `<tbody>`, not an empty-state message — that branch lives one level up in `SourcesPage`), a source whose `config.objects` has one vs many entries (comma-join formatting), and the `SourcesPage` conditional that switches between `SourcesEmptyState` and `SourceTable` plus the `meta`/`actions` text.\n\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"@/components/sources/source-table\";\nimport type { Source } from \"@/types/source\";\n\nconst source = (overrides: Partial<Source> = {}): Source => ({\n  id: \"9c858901-8a57-4791-81fe-4c455b099bc9\",\n  name: \"Prod CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] },\n  createdAt: new Date(),\n  ...overrides,\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders a row per source with joined object list\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source()]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"renders an empty body with no sources\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header only\n  });\n  it(\"renders a single object without a trailing comma\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source({ config: { objects: [\"Account\"] } })]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// app/(console)/sources/page.test.tsx  (integration-ish — mocks the data layer)\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\nimport { listSources } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport SourcesPage from \"@/app/(console)/sources/page\";\n\ndescribe(\"SourcesPage\", () => {\n  it(\"shows the empty state and hides the Add source action when no sources exist\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(listSources).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"No sources yet\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.queryByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Add source\" })).not.toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"shows the table and count once sources exist\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(listSources).mockResolvedValue([{\n      id: \"1\", name: \"CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n      config: { objects: [\"Account\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n    } as any]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"1 configured\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Add source\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### H. `GetStartedPage` — `configured` boolean\n\nUntested boundary: `counts.crm + counts.warehouse + counts.synthetic > 0` flips CTA copy between \"Add your first source\" and \"Continue to sources.\" The `synthetic`-only case is the interesting edge (crm=0, warehouse=0, synthetic=1 → still \"configured\").\n\n```tsx\n// app/get-started/page.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\");\nimport { countSourcesBySide } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport GetStartedPage from \"@/app/get-started/page\";\n\ndescribe(\"GetStartedPage\", () => {\n  it(\"prompts to add a source when nothing is configured\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(countSourcesBySide).mockResolvedValue({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n    render(await GetStartedPage());\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Add your first source\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n  it(\"treats a synthetic-only source as configured\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(countSourcesBySide).mockResolvedValue({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 1 });\n    render(await GetStartedPage());\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Continue to sources\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### I. Missing error handling — Next.js boundaries\n\nThere is **no `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, or `loading.tsx`** anywhere under `app/`. Concretely:\n- `getDb()` throwing (missing `DATABASE_URL`) or `listSources()` throwing (bad row from `sourceSchema.parse`) will currently crash to Next's default unstyled error screen — untested and unhandled.\n- No `loading.tsx` means the `await connection()` + DB round-trip in `SourcesPage`/`GetStartedPage` has no loading UI — nothing enforces one gets added.\n\n```tsx\n// app/(console)/sources/error-boundary.test.tsx (once app/(console)/error.tsx exists)\n// Playwright is a better fit here since Server Component error boundaries\n// don't render meaningfully in RTL/jsdom.\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest(\"shows an error boundary instead of a raw crash when the DB is unreachable\", async ({ page }) => {\n  // requires a way to force DATABASE_URL to point at an unreachable host in test env\n  await page.goto(\"/sources\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(/something went wrong/i)).toBeVisible();\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### J. Integration test gaps (Playwright)\n\nNothing exercises a real browser or a real DB round trip. Suggested minimum suite once Vitest/Playwright are wired up:\n\n1. **Nav flow**: landing (`/`) → Get started → Sources → Sign up, asserting each page renders its header/CTA.\n2. **Sources round trip against a real (test) Postgres**: seed a `sources` row via Drizzle, hit `/sources`, assert the table renders it — this is the only way to catch a `drizzle/0000_organic_black_panther.sql` migration drifting from `lib/db/schema.ts`.\n3. **`getDb()` singleton behavior under Next dev HMR** isn't practically unit-testable — flag it as a manual/smoke check instead of a unit test.\n4. **Cross-schema contract drift**: nothing in this repo currently checks that `types/*.ts` zod schemas stay in sync with `engine/pipeline/schema.py` (explicitly called out in comments as \"mirrors\" and \"change both in the same commit\"). Worth a script that diffs field names/enums between the two, run in CI — not a unit test, but a real gap given how many comments flag it as a manual discipline.\n\n```ts\n// e2e/nav-flow.spec.ts\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest(\"primary navigation flow\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/\");\n  await page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Get started\" }).first().click();\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/get-started/);\n\n  await page.getByRole(\"link\", { name: /sources/i }).click();\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/sources/);\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// e2e/sources-db-roundtrip.spec.ts\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\nimport { getDb } from \"@/lib/db\";\nimport { sources } from \"@/lib/db/schema\";\n\ntest(\"a seeded source appears in the console table\", async ({ page }) => {\n  const db = getDb();\n  await db.insert(sources).values({\n    name: \"Test CRM\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n  });\n\n  await page.goto(\"/sources\");\n  await expect(page.getByText(\"Test CRM\")).toBeVisible();\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of gaps, ranked by risk\n\n| Area | Gap | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| Infra | No test runner at all | Nothing above can run until Vitest/Playwright are added |\n| `lib/db/index.ts` | `getDb()` throw path untested | Only explicit error path in the codebase; currently uncaught anywhere |\n| `lib/server/sources.ts` | `sourceSchema.parse` failure untested | A malformed DB row crashes the page with no boundary |\n| `types/rules.ts` | `.refine` cross-field validation untested | Silent data-integrity gap for `prefer_source` rules |\n| App-wide | No `error.tsx`/`not-found.tsx`/`loading.tsx` | Every thrown error above surfaces as Next's raw crash screen |\n| `types/*.ts` | Schema/engine contract drift unverified | Comments repeatedly flag this as a manual \"change both\" discipline with nothing enforcing it |\n| Components | `SeverityMark`, `NavRail`, `SourceTable` branch logic untested | Small but real conditional logic with no regression protection |\n\nWant me to actually scaffold the Vitest/Playwright config and write these files into the repo, or was this meant purely as an analysis?\n",
